 *  threshold with two decimals ('' when the grade has none: the sheet's applies), dated (keys proof-threshold-A/B/C). `pot` is the pot
 *  with two decimals (not dated; '' when there is none): each member of a balanced pool is shown their cut of it. `parent` is
 *  the parent sheet's id (not dated; '' when there is none): a grade with no rate in force on a date on this sheet takes
 *  the parent's rate for it on that date, then the parent's parent's, up to three levels up. `fiscalStartMonth` is the
 *  month (1 to 12, not dated; 1 unless set) a fiscal year starts on the first day of (see fiscalYearOf). `alertThreshold`
 *  is the alert threshold with two decimals (not dated; '' when off): a person whose due-total crosses above it over a
 *  change is alerted in the audit file. `rounding` is the rounding mode in force (half-up or half-even; '' when none),
 *  dated (key rounding): a claim whose date has one in force rounds its live figures by it, else by the policy date. `reviewThreshold` is the review threshold with two decimals in force ('' when none), dated (key
 *  review-threshold): a claim whose due is above the one in force on its date goes to REVIEW when opened. `escalateAfter` is the escalation gap in days (not dated; '' when off): reminding a
 *  claim whose previous reminder was at least that many days before the sheet's today escalates it, once ever.
 *  `reviewSla` is the review SLA in days (not dated; '' when none): a REVIEW claim whose review day plus it is before
 *  the sheet's today is review-late (see reviewLate). `proofKinds` is the proof kinds, comma separated (not dated; '' when
 *  none): while set, a claim above the proof threshold needs a proof of each listed kind before it can be settled or
 *  approved (the server refuses it). `defaultGrade` is the default grade (A, B or C; not dated; '' when blank, which
 *  means A): the quick-add bar gives a new person it, and an import line with a blank grade uses it.
 *  `gradeClerkLimit` is each grade's own clerk limit with two decimals ('' when the grade has none: the sheet's
 *  applies), dated (keys clerk-limit-A/B/C). `scoreMid` and `scoreHigh` are the score thresholds, whole numbers (not
 *  dated; '' when none): while both are set, each person shows a band (see scoreBand). `scoreLog` is the score log switch (on, or ''
 *  when off; not dated): while on, changing the sheet's today records each person's score on the day being left. `maxOpen` is the maximum of OPEN or
 *  PENDING claims per person, a whole number (not dated; '' when none): opening a claim of a person already at it is
 *  refused (the server refuses it). */
